### Key idea

After PC-1:

```text
56-bit key
     |
     +---- C0 (28 bits)
     |
     +---- D0 (28 bits)
```

For every round:

```text
C(i) = left shift C(i-1)
D(i) = left shift D(i-1)
```

Then:

```text
C(i) || D(i)  →  PC-2  →  48-bit Ki
```

The **first 24 bits of Ki** are selected from the 28-bit `C` half, while the **second 24 bits** are selected from the 28-bit `D` half.

The shift schedule is:

```text
1 1 2 2 2 2 2 2 1 2 2 2 2 2 2 1
```

So DES generates **16 subkeys, each 48 bits**, from the original 64-bit key (8 parity bits are discarded).
